// FILE: artifact_registration_law_v1.law
/*******************************************************************************
 *                           AVIS.ARTIFACT HEADER
 * TYPE: LAW
 * CLASS: REGISTRATION-LAW
 * NAME: ARTIFACT-REGISTRATION-LAW-V1
 * VERSION: 1.00
 * ROLE: Rules for Adding New Artifacts to the AVIS Ecosystem
 * ENGINE: AVIS-2026 / AIFVS-MODE
 * ORIGIN: /mercwar01/law/artifact_registration_law_v1.law
 *******************************************************************************
 * [PURPOSE]
 * Define the process for introducing new artifacts—laws, modules, scripts,
 * structures, or specifications—into the AVIS ecosystem.
 *
 * [REGISTRATION PRINCIPLES]
 * 1. Identity:
 *    Every artifact must have a unique NAME and VERSION.
 *
 * 2. Classification:
 *    Each artifact must declare its TYPE and CLASS.
 *
 * 3. Placement:
 *    Artifacts must specify their canonical filesystem path.
 *
 * 4. Documentation:
 *    Artifacts must include a PURPOSE section.
 *
 * [REGISTRATION PROCESS]
 * Step 1: Assign NAME, TYPE, CLASS, VERSION.
 * Step 2: Define PURPOSE and ROLE.
 * Step 3: Specify ORIGIN path under /mercwar01/.
 * Step 4: Include AVIS.ARTIFACT header.
 * Step 5: Add the artifact to the INDEX registry.
 *
 * [REGISTRY FORMAT]
 * Registry entries must include:
 *   - NAME
 *   - VERSION
 *   - TYPE
 *   - CLASS
 *   - ORIGIN
 *
 * [UPDATE RULES]
 * - Updated artifacts must replace or version‑increment their registry entry.
 *
 * [COMPLIANCE]
 * All new artifacts must follow this law to ensure consistency and
 * discoverability across the AVIS ecosystem.
 *******************************************************************************
 * [END AVIS.ARTIFACT]
 *******************************************************************************/
